{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/656003-question-about-true-friend-merit-and-touchstones","id":656003,"title":"Question about True Friend merit and touchstones","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-07T21:14:39-07:00","id":656003,"title":"Question about True Friend merit and touchstones","content":"Applying the True Friend merit to a touchstone: As it effectively makes the touchstone, being a person, safe from harm (meta), Would you allow this, or is it to too cheese?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/231-blitzburger","name":"Blitzburger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar231_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T21:48:01-07:00","id":656043,"title":"","content":"I'd allow it. It is sort of 'cheese,' but it's the Storyteller who can't kill the True Friend or make them betray you, and I can easily see a vampire PC doing it themselves.<br /> <br /> That said if the player's going to invest in it there's no reason not to abide by it. If a planned story involved a vampire's touchstone betraying them but they got True Friended, I'd suggest changing the story, or asking the player's permission.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T21:55:09-07:00","id":656048,"title":"","content":"Especially since a good part of the Merit's benefits are redundant on a Touchstone. They're basically paying 3 experiences <i>just</i> for that meta protection, since Touchstones can already do everything else a True Friend does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T21:57:39-07:00","id":656051,"title":"","content":"There's no reason you can't have a True Friend Touchstone.<br /> <br /> They aren't inviolate just because of the Merit. The ST isn't supposed to kill them without permission. And the Sanctity of Merit rules of course apply. But there's a bit gap between, &quot;safe from harm,&quot; and, &quot;isn't going to die off without player consent.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T23:34:36-07:00","id":656125,"title":"","content":"Merits can be stacked on a character, so yes you can have a true friend touchstone, and even add retainer or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T23:56:23-07:00","id":656146,"title":"","content":"True Friend even makes it clear that you have to stack it with other things (like Retainer) for it to have any other mechanical impact than what it does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T00:01:35-07:00","id":656161,"title":"","content":"I would have thought the &quot;et cetera&quot; would have clearly including touchstones too for what its worth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T00:49:08-07:00","id":656196,"title":"","content":"Yup. RPing scenes with said True Friend + Touchstone would even add 2 Willpower! Remember that Touchstone are about the choices the character makes. They are not necessarily a sword hanging over the character's neck. While the threat of taking them away *is* a powerful thing, it shouldn't be their only or even primary use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T01:36:24-07:00","id":656220,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I don't like the True Friend merit. Its too meta for my tastes in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T07:43:42-07:00","id":656507,"title":"","content":"I assume Touchstones come with the meta part of True Friend by default as it seems like a waste to go killing them off. No reason to kill off a convenient tool to use against a player. The meta part is okay, but falls flat to me. I guess it might make a player feel better which is enough reason for inclusion. A ST can still cut the arms and legs off of a True Friend, so meh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T15:36:18-07:00","id":657031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/656003-question-about-true-friend-merit-and-touchstones?p=656507#post656507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I assume Touchstones come with the meta part of True Friend by default as it seems like a waste to go killing them off. No reason to kill off a convenient tool to use against a player.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's about just the possibility of losing the touchstone, though, not about actually killing him/her.<br /> <br /> Lets say the antagonist kidnaps the touchstone, and threatens to kill her if the character doesn't meet his demands. With a True Friend Touchstone, the character can just say screw it, retaliate without having to worry about the consequences.<br /> <br /> It may be poor roleplaying, and it may not be a major exploit, but it can certainly change how the player acts.<br /> <br /> And yeah, sure, they could have all their limbs cut off and face melted with acid, but mechanically, it's unimportant.<br /> <br /> Anyways, thanks for the feedback, guys. The topic just kind of sprung to mind last night.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":231,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/231-blitzburger","user":"Blitzburger","date":". 09-08-2015, 10:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/231-blitzburger","name":"Blitzburger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar231_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T20:13:27-07:00","id":657314,"title":"","content":"Oh if a player says &quot;screw it&quot; to an antagonist and &quot;I'll get you back later&quot; allowing the antagonist to horribly maim a Touchstone, the ST should definitely consider that Touchstone lost. The Touchstone won't be dead, but they won't be a Touchstone anymore unless the player can somehow salvage some sort of relationship out of the mess made.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T20:56:21-07:00","id":657334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/656003-question-about-true-friend-merit-and-touchstones?p=657314#post657314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh if a player says &quot;screw it&quot; to an antagonist and &quot;I'll get you back later&quot; allowing the antagonist to horribly maim a Touchstone, the ST should definitely consider that Touchstone lost. The Touchstone won't be dead, but they won't be a Touchstone anymore unless the player can somehow salvage some sort of relationship out of the mess made.</div> </div> </div> </div>They probably won't be a True Friend anymore either. Friends don't abandon friends to their abducters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T07:12:00-07:00","id":657842,"title":"","content":"I don't think a True Friend is supposed to be put in that situation by the GM in the first place, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T09:42:09-07:00","id":658038,"title":"","content":"Why not? True Friends aren't supposed to be killed off by the GM for the sake of the plot. That doesn't leave a True Friend tagged NPC as off-limits for the GM to use as plot material. Going after a vampire's Touchstones (if you can identify them) is a pretty effective indirect way to chip away at a political rival. If your rival falls into the despair of losing those connections (aka the Languid Condition gets applied) they're going to become weaker and weaker; and eventually hit torpor.<br /> <br /> Even if the NPCs threatening your True Friend have no real intention of killing them, they can easily know that you can't the risk of detachment (even if they don't die as Charlaquin points out). The goal might simply to be manipulation.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T13:10:13-07:00","id":658298,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the ST could have a True Friend abducted to direct a player towards or away from a certain action. The player can save the True Friend and do what they want or do what the abductor says. The ST never puts the True Friend at risk of death. If the player decides to not worry about the True Friend because the ST won't kill them off then they are gaming the system. The ST should say okay but you lose the merit and the former friend hates you. That was the choice the player makes. The player put the True Friend's life at risk rather than the ST. I have to think the wording was &quot;kill&quot; rather than &quot;endanger&quot; for a reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T14:55:25-07:00","id":658405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blitzburger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/656003-question-about-true-friend-merit-and-touchstones?p=657031#post657031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's about just the possibility of losing the touchstone, though, not about actually killing him/her.<br /> <br /> Lets say the antagonist kidnaps the touchstone, and threatens to kill her if the character doesn't meet his demands. With a True Friend Touchstone, the character can just say screw it, retaliate without having to worry about the consequences.<br /> <br /> It may be poor roleplaying, and it may not be a major exploit, but it can certainly change how the player acts.<br /> <br /> And yeah, sure, they could have all their limbs cut off and face melted with acid, but mechanically, it's unimportant.<br /> <br /> Anyways, thanks for the feedback, guys. The topic just kind of sprung to mind last night.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not necessarily poor roleplaying, it's equally attributable to shoddy storytelling. The ST is already treading in douchebag territory by having the antagonist target the touchstone and true friend in the first place. <br /> If the PC says &quot;Screw you and the horse you rode in on, I call your bluff you aren't going to kill them.&quot; and refuses to capitulate to the antagonist's demands then it's the ST who created the antagonist who doesn't follow through, or was too shortsighted to create an expanded scenario where the touchstone/true friend is rescued by other parties, not the PC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T15:57:06-07:00","id":658569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/656003-question-about-true-friend-merit-and-touchstones?p=658405#post658405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not necessarily poor roleplaying, it's equally attributable to shoddy storytelling. The ST is already treading in douchebag territory by having the antagonist target the touchstone and true friend in the first place. <br /> If the PC says &quot;Screw you and the horse you rode in on, I call your bluff you aren't going to kill them.&quot; and refuses to capitulate to the antagonist's demands then it's the ST who created the antagonist who doesn't follow through, or was too shortsighted to create an expanded scenario where the touchstone/true friend is rescued by other parties, not the PC.</div> </div> </div> </div>OK, my example wasn't given a lot of thought, but this is kinda what I mean - it essentially takes the touchstone out of play. If the touchstone wasn't a True Friend, their tether to humanity might also become a liability, and personally, I think that's one of the most compelling aspects of the touchstone mechanic. If the ST tries to play on that theme, the player can just yawn, and go shopping, because it's a toothless threat.<br /> <br /> Obviously, STs shouldn't be doing this kind of thing on a regular basis, but when you really want to crank up the drama and urgency, they're a great tool to have in the toolbox.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":231,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/231-blitzburger","user":"Blitzburger","date":". 09-09-2015, 07:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/231-blitzburger","name":"Blitzburger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar231_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T16:26:55-07:00","id":658601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blitzburger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/656003-question-about-true-friend-merit-and-touchstones?p=658569#post658569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> OK, my example wasn't given a lot of thought, but this is kinda what I mean - it essentially takes the touchstone out of play. If the touchstone wasn't a True Friend, their tether to humanity might also become a liability, and personally, I think that's one of the most compelling aspects of the touchstone mechanic. If the ST tries to play on that theme, the player can just yawn, and go shopping, because it's a toothless threat.<br /> <br /> Obviously, STs shouldn't be doing this kind of thing on a regular basis, but when you really want to crank up the drama and urgency, they're a great tool to have in the toolbox.</div> </div> </div> </div>The ST can still put a True Friend in real danger, they just have to discuss it with the player first. Honestly, this is a good policy for any NPCs that the PCs have developed a close relationship with, even if they're not protected by a Merit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T17:17:03-07:00","id":658655,"title":"","content":"You don't have to endanger a touchstone or true friend to use them for drama, sometimes just placing them at risk of witnessing or learning something the character wouldn't want them to know can be enough to force a player to be creative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T12:54:30-07:00","id":659743,"title":"","content":"If you, as an ST, are actively thinking of ways to &quot;get around&quot; True Friend and push the very limits of what you can do without the player being able to point at the rulebook and call foul, you need to take a step back and re-evaluate the relationship between yourself, the rules, and your players. If things are becoming antagonistic, you need to identify the reason why and talk that out with your players. Maybe the True Friend merit is inappropriate for your table. I know in a Changeling game I ran, I asked a player to not take that merit for the express purpose that I didn't want them to feel like any of their connections were &quot;safe&quot; and I felt it undermined the tone I was going for. We talked it out for a bit and came with a compromise that made everyone satisfied.<br /> <br /> In short, if your PC is taking True Friend, challenge yourself to find ways to make that relationship interesting and stressful without pouring acid on someone's face. In fact, I'd say that in general you should explore ways to entertain yourself that doesn't involve pouring acid on people's faces. It's just polite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T15:11:29-07:00","id":659954,"title":"","content":"I think the acid on the face was hyperbole, but I agree with the sentiment there.<br /> <br /> It was never about getting around True Friend. The problem was stated as a player gaming the system by using the no kill element as a means not to role-play. A True Friend should be at risk by virtue of having a close relationship with a player character that has enemies. The fact that the ST should not consider killing the True Friend without the player's permission creates a &quot;safe&quot; environment. When a True Friend is kidnapped, the player knows they can do something about it that won't lead to the True Friend's death. If the player refuses to do anything the they have forfeited the relationship. Taking it out on the True Friend is convenient for explanations, but really the point of the ST should be to let the player know they gave up the merit by their choice.<br /> <br /> You see the scenario in movies. The protagonist's little buddy is kidnapped to coerce an action without any defined threat. The friend is held until the protagonist does what they are told. The protagonist can do as directed, save their friend, or get help. The friend is never truly in danger in a meta sense and depending on the circumstances even in the story there might be no danger. All this is well within the rules. A player would be wrong to take the merit to prevent such things.<br /> <br /> I think touchstones should always get that treatment. Others might disagree. That would be the point discussions should be made. Players shouldn't take the merit to try to limit story ideas short of *bam* your friend is dead, now what? If a player doesn't want the kind of story where player character friends are put in danger that needs to get worked out without merits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T15:56:49-07:00","id":659985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/656003-question-about-true-friend-merit-and-touchstones?p=659743#post659743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you, as an ST, are actively thinking of ways to &quot;get around&quot; True Friend and push the very limits of what you can do without the player being able to point at the rulebook and call foul, you need to take a step back and re-evaluate the relationship between yourself, the rules, and your players. If things are becoming antagonistic, you need to identify the reason why and talk that out with your players. Maybe the True Friend merit is inappropriate for your table. I know in a Changeling game I ran, I asked a player to not take that merit for the express purpose that I didn't want them to feel like any of their connections were &quot;safe&quot; and I felt it undermined the tone I was going for. We talked it out for a bit and came with a compromise that made everyone satisfied.<br /> <br /> In short, if your PC is taking True Friend, challenge yourself to find ways to make that relationship interesting and stressful without pouring acid on someone's face. In fact, I'd say that in general you should explore ways to entertain yourself that doesn't involve pouring acid on people's faces. It's just polite.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is why I love the True Friend Merit. Just by existing, it encourages healthy ST and Player relationships and open communication.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T17:55:46-07:00","id":660144,"title":"","content":"I'm sure it was hyperbole and do not have reason to believe any member of these forums would actually entertain themselves by dumping acid on people's faces. I was playing off the absurdity for kicks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T20:06:32-07:00","id":660256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/656003-question-about-true-friend-merit-and-touchstones?p=659954#post659954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think touchstones should always get that treatment.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've seen this sentiment a few times in this thread. I'm going to have to be one of the people that disagree.<br /> <br /> The Touchstone shouldn't be untouchable. There are aspects of a vampire's story that you can't really examine any other way than be threatening or even killing the Touchstone. It highlights how tenuous their connection to humanity is. Their death lets the group examine how the character reacts to that kind of deep loss. How they act without a leash to restrain them. How they might try getting another one, or if they even bother.<br /> <br /> Abusing this can lead to problems, surely, but as a once-in-a-campaign trauma, it can be very potent to lose a Touchstone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T20:39:23-07:00","id":660275,"title":"","content":"The treatment being give the player a chance to save a touchstone if they want and don't go killing them off unless the player is okay with it. Definitely don't kill them off without a meaningful reason. I think one of the purposes of a touchstone is for it to be threatened. Still I don't doubt some would disagree with this treatment. That's fine, but I think people should work out how they want to play rather than rely on a merit if everyone isn't on the same page. True Friend shouldn't be reduced to a way to keep an asset from dying. Too high a cost for what should be resolved with a discussion between ST and player.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}